[{"id":16562,"sender_id":12,"sender_full_name":"Eric","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2d29383a45071e6fd2765d3c6b7f4bca?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Technical.3A.20.24.3E.24.20not.20rendering/near/16562\">#1</a> It looks like some problems with David’s <a href=\"http://www.math.ntnu.no/~stacey/Mathforge/nForum/comments.php?DiscussionID=1900&amp;Focus=16585#Comment_16585\">recent comment</a></p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&gt;</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>The “&gt;” symbol in itex is probably getting confused with HTML or something.</p>","timestamp":1285917152,"subject":"Technical: $>$ not rendering","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":16573,"sender_id":9,"sender_full_name":"Andrew Stacey","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/59e0a28758c4f6630d67fe7138b37311?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Technical.3A.20.24.3E.24.20not.20rendering/near/16573\">#2</a> The symbols “&gt;” and “&lt;” are not valid iTeX.  You should always use <code>\\lt</code> and <code>\\gt</code> to get them: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x \\lt y</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y \\gt x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7335em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span>.  It’s one of the few differences between iTeX and LaTeX.</p>","timestamp":1285924301,"subject":"Technical: $>$ not rendering","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":16576,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Technical.3A.20.24.3E.24.20not.20rendering/near/16576\">#3</a> Thanks, I’ll change my comment.</p>","timestamp":1285924942,"subject":"Technical: $>$ not rendering","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]}]